  "pedal": "Boss GE-7 Equalizer — focused reamp: guitar excerpts for the fit and the scorecard (mono)",
  "comment": "Short excerpts of the guitar DI dataset (captures/di/), chosen so each take shows one thing in the model on real guitar. chords (25 s of strummed open chords: the widest spectrum) gives each setting's response where a guitar has energy; funk (12 s, the dataset's hottest peaks) on a level ladder (-24/-12/0 dB) separates the linear EQ from the ceiling: at Level +15 (the ceiling 15 dB sooner, after Level) and with every band at +15 (the stages before Level); the same take twice (mid-boost-funk and -repeat) gives the pedal's difference from itself, the floor for every number; the lead excerpts are held out of any fit, as the check. chugs: the low strings on the scoop's 100/200 Hz boost. Sliders on the printed marks. Takes ordered for the fewest slider moves: flat, Level alone twice, then three shapes.",
